  "id": "read-update-sequence-idempotent-retry",
  "description": "A sequence whose client disconnected after admission, so its response was lost. A concurrent identical retry meets the first member in flight: that member and its dependent fail transiently and claim nothing, while an unrelated third member runs. After the delay the sequence is retried byte-identically, then with a new member in front, then with all three members: every retained disposition is returned without re-execution — the allocated identities and revisions never change — positioned by the present member's operationIndex and operationName. Conditions are narrated, not observed. Illustrative wire example; not evidence.",
